{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"This pub is the center of life for the locals who live and work in the city. The Ale is cold and the food is hot.\n\nA persuasion check might get you access to the back room.\n\nA shady character with a mask that has no face ushers you into a room. There, guns are laid out, in no particular item.\n\n\"You're gonna use it for home defense, right?\"","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:18:51.784000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T06:35:54.888000Z","id":"863303239873331220","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"Misty Shot\nFirearm- Pistol (rare): 10, 000 gold\nThis Misty Shot pistol seems to always have a small amount of smoke streaming from its barrel. This magic firearm has a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls and deals an extra 1d8 force damage. Twice per day you may use the Misty Shot to cast Misty Step, changing the range to match the pistols range.\n\nBuckler Bow \nUncommon Shortbow: 2100 gold\nEquipped with a small buckler this bow gives the wielder a little extra defense and some offense should an enemy get to close. This bow gives you a +1 to your AC while wielding it and you can use the blunt side of the shield to make a melee attack at a creature within 5ft of you dealing 1d4 bludgeoning damage.\n\nIf an enemy makes a melee attack at you, you may use your reaction to add 1d4 AC for that attack. This must be used before you know if the attack hits.\n\nHeavier Crossbow\n\nHeavy, Loading, Range, Two-handed\nRare\nRequires at least 16 Strength\n\nThis heavy crossbow has been modified to fire javelins. It has an extra set of limbs to help fire the javelins and the stock rests on the wielder’s shoulder. \n\nThe Heavier Crossbow deals 2d10+1d6 piercing damage. Before taking the attack action with the Heavier Crossbow you must aim at the target using your bonus action. You only need to aim once per turn. It can be loaded with up to 3 javelins into the three chamber loader. Even with the Crossbow Expert feat you still need to spend an action loading the javelin.","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:19:40.127000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T11:14:56.326000Z","id":"863303442637127691","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"Blazing Bess\nFirearm, two-handed\nRare:  17, 000\nWhen tasked by the general to design a new firearm, the artificer took his meaning all too literally and thus the Blazing Bess was born. A canister of alchemist’s fire has been retrofitted to the barrel of the gun and set up to shoot more “hot” than lead. The canister has 6 charges and requires help from an artificer to refuel over a short rest. Above the trigger there is a switch that can alternate the firing modes, Heat Wave and Scorcher. Changing the mode requires bonus action.\n\nAs an action you can spend one of the charges in the following ways.\n\nHeat Wave: A short range blast of flames sears nearby enemies. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must make a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 2d6 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. \n\nScorcher: A long blast of flames shoots out 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 2d8 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:22:08.446000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T08:43:38.614000Z","id":"863304064732102706","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"Volt Thrower \nFirearm (chaingun) \nAmmunition (range 50/150), burst fire only, heavy, two-handed\nVery Rare: 10, 000\nBy this point the General had been raised up to having control over most of the surrounding lands. He approached the artificer with a gleam of arrogance and commanded he be made a weapon that the Gods themselves would kneel to and truly show his dominion over all. As always the Artificer went right to work, a gleam in his eye.\n\nA large platinum multi barreled gun attached to a  hefty ammo pack, slung over shoulders with thick metal chains, was the result of his work. The barrels crackle with electricity as the gun spins up. While attuned to this you have resistance to lightning damage.\n\nSpin Up\nBefore you make a burst attack with the chaingun, it must spin up. This takes a bonus action. Once the chaingun is spinning, it remains spinning until the end of your next turn in which you do not attack with it.\n\nLightning Shackles \nBolts of lightning spray from the barrels as you pull the trigger on the spun up gun. You choose up to 5 targets that are all within at least 15 feet of one of the other targets. They must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 4d8 Lightning damage and are restrained as the electric current surges through their body’s, or half as much and suffer no other ill effects on a success.\n\nStatic Burst\nAs a reaction to getting hit by an attack and as long as the chaingun is spun up, you can make all creatures within 5ft of you make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. Taking 2d8 lightning damage and disadvantage on the next attack they make on a failure or half as much and no disadvantage on a success. After using this you need to Spin Up again.","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:23:15.164000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T11:16:39.218000Z","id":"863304344567939113","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"Palm Pistol \nWeapon, common\nAttack Type: Ranged\nRange: 40ft./160ft.\nDamage: 1d8\nDamage Type: Piercing\nWeight: 1lb.\nCost: 50 gp\nProperties: Light, Reload (6), Misfire (1)\n\nReload. The weapon can be fired a number of times equal to its Reload score before you must spend 1 attack or 1 action to reload. You must have one free hand to reload a firearm.\n\nMisfire. Whenever you make an attack roll with a firearm, and score a natural 1. The attack misses, and the weapon cannot be used again until you spend an action to try and repair it. To repair your firearm, you must make a successful Tinker’s Tools check (DC equal to 8 + misfire score). If your check fails, the weapon is broken and must be mended out of combat at a quarter of the cost of the firearm. Creatures who use a firearm without being proficient increase the weapon’s misfire score by 1.\n\nAmmunition\nAll firearms require ammunition to make an attack.\n\nPistol\nWeapon, common\nAttack Type:\nRanged\nRange: 30ft./90ft.\nDamage: 1d10\nDamage Type:\n Piercing\nWeight: 3lb.\nCost: 250 gp\nProperties: Properties: Light, Reload (9), Misfire (1)\nAmmunition (Firearms), Range, Loading,  Ammunition\n\nReload. The weapon can be fired a number of times equal to its Reload score before you must spend 1 attack or 1 action to reload. You must have one free hand to reload a firearm.\n\nMisfire. Whenever you make an attack roll with a firearm, and score a natural 1. The attack misses, and the weapon cannot be used again until you spend an action to try and repair it. To repair your firearm, you must make a successful Tinker’s Tools check (DC equal to 8 + misfire score). If your check fails, the weapon is broken and must be mended out of combat at a quarter of the cost of the firearm. Creatures who use a firearm without being proficient increase the weapon’s misfire score by 1.\n\nAll firearms require ammunition to make an attack.","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:30:11.331000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T06:50:21.757000Z","id":"863306090100162600","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"860473039098740766","content":"Revolver\nWeapon, common\nAttack Type: Ranged\nRange: 40ft./120ft.\nDamage: 2d8\nDamage Type: Piercing\nWeight: 3lb.\nCost: 50 gp\n\nProperties:\nAmmunition (Firearms), Range, Reload\nReload. The weapon can be fired a number of times equal to its Reload score before you must spend 1 attack or 1 action to reload. You must have one free hand to reload a firearm.\n\nMisfire. Whenever you make an attack roll with a firearm, and score a natural 1. The attack misses, and the weapon cannot be used again until you spend an action to try and repair it. To repair your firearm, you must make a successful Tinker’s Tools check (DC equal to 8 + misfire score). If your check fails, the weapon is broken and must be mended out of combat at a quarter of the cost of the firearm. Creatures who use a firearm without being proficient increase the weapon’s misfire score by 1.","created_at":"2021-07-10T06:32:32.335000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T06:47:41.261000Z","id":"863306681513803796","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
